/// REFUSE: 'Circle' is exported by units 'Round' and 'Flat'; qualify it.
///
/// Issue #18.  Importing two units that export one name is legal; using the
/// bare name is not, and the error belongs where the name is USED rather than
/// where the units are imported -- importing costs nothing until a program
/// actually writes the ambiguous name.
///
/// ⚠️ The sentence here is proposed rather than observed.  Today the program is
/// refused at the second 'uses' with ''Circle'' is already defined; mark it
/// private in one of the modules', which is the defect: it refuses the import
/// rather than the use, and advises avoiding the collision rather than naming
/// which one is meant.
///
uses '../lib/Round';
uses '../lib/Flat';

begin
    WriteLn (Circle ().Kind ());
end
